Upstream
This project began as a fork of BetaSuite 0.2.4 by solarorb93, with
thanks for the original idea and work:
https://github.com/solarorb93/BetaSuite

The upstream repository carries no license file, and permission to
license its code was requested and not answered. Every part of this
repository that came from it has since been removed or replaced by code
written independently from descriptions of the required behavior,
without access to the upstream code. What remains
in common is what any implementation must share: names that other code
calls, model tensor names and class order fixed by the model files, and
library calls and data values the behavior requires.

The repository's history from before that rewrite still contains the
upstream code. It remains under its author's rights, and the license in
LICENSE grants nothing for it.

Third-party components
The project hosts the detection and segmentation models the app downloads,
as files of a GitHub release (listed with their hashes in
assets/models/catalog.json). Each keeps its own license, published beside
it with a NOTICE, and the upstream source each was converted from (the .pt,
.pth or training checkpoint) is hosted beside it unchanged. They are used
through onnxruntime; BetaSuite's own environment includes neither PyTorch
nor the packages the models were trained or exported with.

- NudeNet (https://github.com/notAI-tech/NudeNet). The 320n and 640m
  detectors, from its v3.4-weights release, are AGPL-3.0 (its license at
  that tag); its README describes them as based on Ultralytics YOLOv8n and
  YOLOv8m. The RetinaNet detector, from its v0 release, is GPL-3.0 (its
  license at that tag), which AGPL-3.0 section 13 allows to be combined
  with this project.
- Ultralytics YOLO11-seg (https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics):
  the n, s and m person models, exported to ONNX from the v8.3.0 release
  weights, are AGPL-3.0.
- RF-DETR-Seg by Roboflow (https://github.com/roboflow/rf-detr): the nano,
  small and medium person models, exported to ONNX from the published
  weights, are Apache-2.0.
